   "body": "**cloud/i884-sonnet** — finding, no PR opened (base `d683644`).\n\nTL;DR: in the code, the editor text size already equals the reader's. I found no code-level cause, and a change I can't tie to one would be a guess.\n\n**What I checked**\n- Editor: `ComposerEditorCard.swift:59-60` applies `.scaledFont(.body)`. That is `TextScale.font(.body, at: dynamicTypeSize)`: `UIFont.preferredFont(.body, compatibleWith: DT size).pointSize × percent/100` (`Settings/TextScale.swift`). The measuring copy of the text (`textMeasure`) uses the same modifier. `.scaledFont(.body)` was added in #849 (2026-11-12), the day before this issue was filed, so the issue describes the build with that rule already in.\n- Reader: `reader.css:60-62`, `html { font: -apple-system-body }` and `body { font-size: calc(var(--text-scale) * 1rem) }`. `.content` sets no `font-size` of its own, so the message text is body × scale. Same rule, same factor (`ReaderWebController.textScaleScript`).\n- Legacy (`AnswerView.swift` `ReplyTextEditor.editorFont` @ 87fe0d1c, via `AppTextSizeScale.scaledUIFont`, `Common.swift:314-322`): `UIFontMetrics(.body).scaledFont(UIFont.systemFont(ofSize: 17 × factor))`. Same point size as the Swift rule.\n- Nothing between the app root (`appTypography`) and the editor overrides `textScale` or `dynamicTypeSize`; both composer paths (sheet and docked) go through `ComposerEditorCard`.\n\n**So the 2026-11-13 device observation is not explained by the code.** Candidates I can't test on Linux:\n1. `TextEditor` not honouring the fixed-size `.system(size:)` font (the font set by `.font` may not reach the underlying text view), or the reader's rendered size differing from the CSS rule (viewport, `-webkit-text-size-adjust`).\n2. The build tested predating #849.\n3. A perceived difference from line height or theme font, not point size.\n\n**What would settle it (Mac, one check):** on a device or simulator at in-app 100 % and 150 %, read the editor's `UITextView.font.pointSize` (debugger) and the reader's computed `.content` `font-size` (`getComputedStyle`), and say whether the editor is still smaller on a build with #849. If the sizes differ, the fix is in the editor's font plumbing; if they match, the issue is line height or font family and needs a new description.\n\nI have not changed code and left `fix/884-composer-text-size` unpushed. Say if you want me to add the regression test alone (editor font == reader rule at 80/100/150 %), which would pass today and guard the rule, or to wait for the device measurement.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
